WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:01.067
As if the

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.068
first ever indictment

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:02.836
of a former president

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.070
wasn't enough to digest.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:04.537
This week,

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.172
Tennessee pushed the political world

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.707
into a further tailspin.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.376
The GOP dominated House

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.510
voting to expel two young

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.544
Democratic lawmakers

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:12.946
because they had taken part

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.948
in a gun control protest.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.116
It didn't escape.

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:17.317
Notice that Representatives

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.619
Justin Jones and Justin Pearson are black

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:20.487
while they're white collar.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:21.521
Gloria Johnson

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:22.522
also protested,

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:24.324
but she survived being kicked out

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:25.225
by one vote.

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.426
And joining us now to talk about

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:27.360
this is Republican

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.195
strategist, CNN political analyst

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:29.763
Alice Stewart,

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.031
and CNN political commentator

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.198
Bakari Sellers,

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.367
a former South Carolina state legislator.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:35.335
Bakari.

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:36.302
I have to start with you first,

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.804
because I got to wonder

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.239
what would have been like for you

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.174
to be in the thick of this?

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.208
How did we get here?

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.013
That's a good question.

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.481
And how would I have felt to be

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.082
in the thick of this?

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.484
I don't think that at the period of time

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:54.921
I like that from 2006 to 2014,

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.924
the temperature was what it is today.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.960
The fact is, I think Republicans

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.362
in the Tennessee General

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:02.762
Assembly

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.864
just shot themselves in the foot.

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.033
They didn't want these young black men.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.068
They probably looked at them

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:09.402
as these young colored boys

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:10.336
be able to speak up

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:12.272
and use their use their words

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.640
and use their courage.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.542
And do the things that they felt

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.277
should be done.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:19.446
But yet and still they made them martyrs.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.047
They put them on a pedestal.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.116
Now, everybody knows just an injustice

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.751
And the fact they did it

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:25.919
without any regard

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.720
to their white colleague, Gloria,

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.055
who's actually an ally,

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:30.824
who is a hero herself.

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:32.692
It just shows you what this was about.

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:35.695
This was about putting two young Negroes

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:36.463
in their place.

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.664
And I think it backfired

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:39.732
and let in 1966 and Julian Bond.

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:42.235
And Alice

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:42.902
that state

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:43.970
legislator that

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.505
Bakari just mentioned Gloria Johnson

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.372
she said yes

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:47.941
because of the color of my skin

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.043
that she was spared and the other two

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.778
lawmakers were not

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.346
when it comes to expulsion

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:54.481
Let me ask you, Alice.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.883
The Republican Party in Tennessee

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.985
they hold a supermajority

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.221
in the General Assembly there.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.956
Is this what you wanted to see this week

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:06.693
from state lawmakers there in Tennessee.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:07.861
Was this a mistake?

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:08.962
Did they go too far?

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.029
What do you think

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.800
It is not what I wanted to see.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.535
Yes, they made a mistake and yes,

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:16.469
they went too far.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:17.971
I think this absolutely

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.139
could have been handled

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:22.842
by just censuring these legislators

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:25.145
and potentially maybe removing them

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:26.713
from their committee assignments.

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:28.314
And they certainly would have

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.115
gotten the message.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:29.983
And I've spoken

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.284
with one of the

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:33.720
representatives that made this decision,

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.221
and they said it was very difficult.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.023
It was a very emotional day.

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.758
But when they looked at the footage

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.393
and talked with people

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:40.960
that were there

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.629
on the day of these protests,

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:44.697
they saw the two justins

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.700
acting a little bit more aggressively

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.336
than the woman who was not expelled

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.038
from the legislature.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.907
They saw them going up into the balcony

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:56.976
and inciting the crowd and really

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.612
furthering the intensity

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:00.580
of these protests.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.080
And look,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.315
I give all three of them

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.116
great courage

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:04.117
for standing up

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.186
for what they believe in and standing up

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:06.819
for what

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.321
they want to see

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.356
in terms of enacting legislation.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.225
But many people know

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:13.793
and Bakari knows this,

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.195
having been in the legislature,

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:17.063
in order to effect change

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:19.165
and have meaningful legislative outcomes,

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:21.134
you need to have common ground.

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:22.001
You need to have

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:22.936
communication,

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:24.604
you need to have civil discourse

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:25.638
on these issues.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:28.141
And in order to change legislation,

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.309
you have to change

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:30.443
hearts and minds

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:32.912
and make meaningful legislation.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:35.381
And I truly believe if these three had

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:38.218
tried to have meaningful conversations

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.752
with all of the legislature,

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:40.853
about meaningful ways

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.488
to reform gun violence,

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.257
that could have been helpful

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.593
and certainly would have made progress.

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:47.927
Unfortunately,

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:50.230
this is still the first of what I see

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.031
many, many more conversations

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:54.000
from the three of these people.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:54.834
And Bakari,

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:55.501
what do you see

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.936
in terms of this

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:59.138
being an assault on democracy?

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:01.507
At the state level in Tennessee?

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.543
Did you view it that way?

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:04.410
I know a lot of folks

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.878
in the Democratic Party,

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:08.147
they see sort of a rollback of

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.818
I guess, democratic

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:13.753
procedures taking place in statehouses

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.154
across the country.

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.322
Is that what you did?

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:16.990
You see some of that

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:20.059
at play in Tennessee as well?

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:21.527
I did, Jim.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:21.961
And, you know,

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.129
people always want to say

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:25.131
I mean, as soon as we get out this office

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:26.766
segment, people are going to say,

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:27.267
what are you

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.501
why are you playing the race card?

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.503
On social media is going to go crazy?

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:31.871
Well, you have to understand the dynamics

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:33.273
of where we are in the South.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:34.173
You have to understand

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.808
the dynamics of these

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:38.111
these young black men

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:40.613
attempting to speak their truth to power.

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:42.315
You have to understand

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.049
the dynamics

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:45.084
of what's at play in Nashville,

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:45.785
where you have

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:47.520
these kind of democratic epicenters

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.855
of economic

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:50.423
empowerment in Memphis

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:51.724
where these men represent.

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:52.892
And so when you

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.961
when you put all of these things together

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:55.995
and you see the fact

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:57.630
that the first thing they wanted to do

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:58.831
was shut them up.

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.033
The first thing they wanted to do

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:00.967
was tell them that,

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:02.702
boy, you can't speak no more,

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:05.838
then you realize where we truly are.

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:07.373
I mean, you think about Josh Hawley.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:07.573
I mean,

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.175
people want to talk about decorum.

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:10.710
You think about Josh Hawley

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.645
raising his fist of power

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.781
as he walks by insurrectionist.

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:15.782
And Josh Hawley

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.750
today is still a United States senator

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.086
from the great state of Missouri.

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:21.354
Like people never thought

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:23.323
about removing him from office.

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:24.257
But we had young

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.792
people gunned down in a school.

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:28.027
Let's put all of this in the context

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.495
we had young people, babies

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.130
gunned down in a school.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.633
And these young people, these young black

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.635
boys, men, excuse me, decided

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:37.370
they were going to

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.137
speak their truth

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:38.671
to power

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.239
about not having any more

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:42.275
young babies gunned down.

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:44.944
And yet they eject them from their seats.

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:46.579
And so there's something else

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:47.480
at play here.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.048
And I think what's at play is race.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:51.050
I think power dynamics are at play.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.652
And I think the erosion of democracy,

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:54.220
as you said, Jim, is at play.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.521
And until we truly deal

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:56.489
with these things,

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:57.123
Donald Trump

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:58.358
showed us that you can use

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:00.326
racism as political currency.

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:01.494
You can attempt to chip away

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:02.995
at a road democracy.

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:04.430
And then you can talk to people

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.065
however you want to talk to them

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:07.867
and still be politically successful

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:08.935
in this country.

00:06:08.935 --> 00:06:10.370
That's the danger.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.637
And that's why we understand

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.706
democracy is fragile.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:14.807
And Alice

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:16.542
McCarthy brings up a good point.

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:17.610
Sure. Go ahead. Go ahead.

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:20.513
Now, if I could just say,

00:06:20.513 --> 00:06:21.914
having worked in the state house

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:23.883
right across the border from Tennessee

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:25.118
in Little Rock,

00:06:25.118 --> 00:06:26.219
in the governor's office,

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:27.520
and seeing how

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.390
legislative proceedings are carried out,

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:33.259
there are rules.

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:34.193
There are

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.661
there's procedural,

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:37.964
the quorum that is necessary

00:06:37.964 --> 00:06:40.066
in order to make meaningful change

00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:42.201
to represent people all across the state.

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:43.202
And the

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:44.504
those that I have spoken with

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:46.672
say when you violate those norms,

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:48.141
there needs to be consequences.

00:06:48.141 --> 00:06:50.510
And we need to have order in order

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.645
to make change in these states.

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:53.713
And again,

00:06:53.713 --> 00:06:54.714
I can't say

00:06:54.714 --> 00:06:56.215
I commend these three

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:58.017
for standing up for what they want to do.

00:06:58.017 --> 00:06:59.051
But the best way

00:06:59.051 --> 00:07:00.453
to have meaningful change

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:02.522
and get back to the real topic at hand

00:07:02.755 --> 00:07:04.524
is these six innocent lives

00:07:04.524 --> 00:07:06.426
that were killed in the school shooting.

00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:08.394
How do we prevent this from happening?

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:10.129
Let's hear from the Tennessee three.

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:11.864
Let's talk about red flag laws.

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:13.566
Let's talk about hardening targets.

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:15.601
Let's talk about school resource officers

00:07:16.469 --> 00:07:17.303
about mental health.

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:18.571
All of these ideas

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:19.605
from legislators

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:20.840
across the state of Tennessee

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:21.741
in the country

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:22.975
are important

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:25.011
to have meaningful gun violence change.

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:25.778
But Alice,

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:26.412
I mean, didn't

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:27.079
Marjorie Taylor

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:28.448
Greene violate

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:29.382
some decorum

00:07:29.382 --> 00:07:30.750
during the State of the Union speech

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:31.451
for President Biden

00:07:31.451 --> 00:07:33.019
when she was shouting liar at him?

00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:33.719
I mean, she's done this

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:35.822
a couple of State of the unions in a row.

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:39.692
And, you know, she wasn't kicked out

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:43.029
that.

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:46.132
Marjorie Taylor Greene is

00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:47.333
on her own island

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:48.501
and she has been kicked off

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.069
committee assignments in the past.

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:50.269
And look,

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:51.604
I think there's a completely

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:52.305
there's a

00:07:52.305 --> 00:07:53.573
slightly different scenario

00:07:53.573 --> 00:07:55.908
when she inappropriately

00:07:55.908 --> 00:07:58.311
and disrespectfully screams out

00:07:58.311 --> 00:07:59.912
at the president of the United States.

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:01.147
I think that is absolutely,

00:08:01.147 --> 00:08:02.248
completely wrong.

00:08:02.248 --> 00:08:03.850
But this is a different situation,

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.151
in my view,

00:08:05.151 --> 00:08:06.686
when you have legislators

00:08:06.686 --> 00:08:07.587
that have disrupted

00:08:07.587 --> 00:08:08.821
the legislative process

00:08:08.821 --> 00:08:10.490
for nearly an hour

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.692
and were given the opportunity to say,

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:13.159
all right,

00:08:13.159 --> 00:08:14.560
let's have conversations

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:16.896
and we won't do that in the future

00:08:16.896 --> 00:08:18.130
when that didn't happen.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:18.965
That's why

00:08:18.965 --> 00:08:20.800
these legislators in Tennessee

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.269
made the decision they had.

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:24.737
All right.

00:08:24.804 --> 00:08:26.973
Last word from you, Bakari.

00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:29.342
Yeah, I mean, I think that I mean,

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:31.410
with respect to Alice and everyone else,

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.379
we saw John Lewis, the great John Lewis,

00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:34.380
take a seat on the state

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:35.414
on the on the floor

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:36.916
of the United States Congress.

00:08:36.916 --> 00:08:38.584
We see these acts of civil

00:08:38.584 --> 00:08:40.853
disobedience happen all the time.

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:42.755
It's civil disobedience.

00:08:42.755 --> 00:08:44.090
They broke no laws.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:45.458
They committed no crimes.

00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:47.093
They violated decorum.

00:08:47.093 --> 00:08:48.628
In a general assembly,

00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:50.696
committed acts of civil disobedience.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:52.064
And yet you have lawmakers

00:08:52.064 --> 00:08:53.099
who actually violate

00:08:53.099 --> 00:08:54.166
real crimes,

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:55.067
commit DUIs,

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:57.003
who beat their wives, etc., etc.

00:08:57.003 --> 00:08:58.638
and they still get a chance to sit.

00:08:58.638 --> 00:09:00.339
So let's actually add

00:09:00.339 --> 00:09:01.207
context to this

00:09:01.207 --> 00:09:02.341
and understand what they did in

00:09:02.341 --> 00:09:03.442
Tennessee was about

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:05.011
race, was about power,

00:09:05.011 --> 00:09:06.579
and was about eroding democracy.

00:09:06.579 --> 00:09:07.413
Shame on Tennessee.

